# Project Context: Azzurro Hotels — Booking.com Review Insights Dashboard

## Business Context
- Client: Azzurro Hotels Pty Ltd (Sydney), pod/boutique hospitality.
- Default properties (swap if portal specifies different four):
  1. Azzurro Pod Hotel Darling Harbour — 22 Allen St, Pyrmont
  2. Azzurro Pod Hotel Central Sydney — 90 Wentworth Ave
  3. Azzurro Pod Hotel Potts Point — 141–143 Victoria St
  4. Azzurro Boutique Hotel Surry Hills — 84 Flinders St
- Goal: Ops + executive dashboard that turns Booking.com guest feedback into actionable daily tasks.

## Tech Stack
- Next.js App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS
- Charts: Recharts | Icons: Lucide
- AI via Route Handlers (`/api/insights`, `/api/reply`) + deterministic fallback
- Deploy: Vercel | Data: structured JSON/CSV (no required DB for demo)

## Core Features
1. Property switcher (All + each property)
2. KPI row: overall rating (0–10) + trend, review count, response rate, unreplied negatives, sentiment
3. Booking.com category scores: Staff, Cleanliness, Location, Facilities, Comfort, Value
4. Monthly rating / volume trend
5. AI ops insights + prioritized action items for onsite staff
6. Draft reply on individual reviews
7. Searchable/filterable review explorer
8. CSV / data-source panel for ingest readiness

## Coding Standards
- Components under `src/components/dashboard/`
- Types under `src/lib/types.ts`, data under `src/data/`
- Hospitality-ops UI: slate/neutral, clear status badges, responsive
- Prefer working polish over over-engineering
- Never commit secrets or `_trial-notes/`
